Section 1353. A person may lead his cattle into or through
another person's unenclosed land for grazing and watering;
he may fetch water from a well or pound within such land;
provided always that it is not a plantation and is not
prepared for cultivation, sown or covered with a crop. The
owner may however forbid such action.

Section 1566. A child is subject to parental power as long
as he is not sui juris.
The parental power is exercised by the father or the mother
in any of the following cases;
1. the mother or the father is dead; 
2. It is uncertain whether the mother or t he father is living
or dead; 
